dependent vectors that can be removed. Here, the $1$st and $3$rd columns are pivot columns, while the $2$nd column is a non-pivot column.\n\nThe $1$st and $3$rd columns from the original matrix are ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{3}.$ So, a basis of $S$ is ${{a}_{1},{a}_{3}},$ that is to say, \n\n$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120326 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6f644bed-7adb-5907-87b4-99b1902e7850" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Basis of the Space Spanned by a Set of Vectors by Identifying Pivot Columns"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "671d8054-3319-5866-97a1-76fef64ba3ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B={[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348964} {:answer/id #uuid "c395728a-602c-578c-8f62-b24acf6684ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B={[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348965} {:answer/id #uuid "b6b13ddc-037a-5c78-b23e-615cbd0340b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B={[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348966} {:answer/id #uuid "6e24140a-d221-5ea9-ad45-24ee777875d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B={[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348967} {:answer/id #uuid "6b503919-4dc0-54d9-b89e-d58a8c8fd0d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B={[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348968}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c395728a-602c-578c-8f62-b24acf6684ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B={[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348965} :answer-field/id #uuid "7fdfa577-030a-577a-ad88-5f9142aa0fdb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348963}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6fe4864a-ed27-50fc-8816-ad1ec4b0dfc8" :question/math-academy-id "q-35694" :question/problem "Consider the vectors ${a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],$ ${a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}],$ and ${a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].$ Find a basis $B$ of $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}.$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find a subset of linearly independent vectors. So, we start by creating a matrix whose columns are made up of our vectors, and then we reduce the matrix to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 3 & -6 & -3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+\\frac{3}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -6\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe pivot columns correspond to linearly independent vectors, while the non-pivot columns correspond to linearly dependent vectors that can be removed. Here, the $1$st and $3$rd columns are pivot columns, while the $2$nd column is a non-pivot column.\n\nRemember that we need to pick the pivot columns from the *original matrix*, not from the reduced one.\n\nThe $1$st and $3$rd columns from the original matrix are ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{3}.$ So, a basis of $S$ is ${{a}_{1},{a}_{3}},$ that is to say, \n\n$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348969 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f892805c-2c2c-5105-91ba-353aefe7b7f2" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Basis of the Space Spanned by a Set of Vectors Using Inspection"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fbb1f07b-43df-5dbc-a5d5-ac2bff3b18f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B={[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348971} {:answer/id #uuid "604450ec-7083-5075-b744-5e30a92dc7c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348972} {:answer/id #uuid "56ffda48-82e0-5e51-80c3-b5e74877dbca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B={[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348973} {:answer/id #uuid "31461327-860d-5375-afd7-a192d9de0764" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B={[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348974} {:answer/id #uuid "3c73fe48-fdfc-55bb-b7f0-f6cb69927767" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B={[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348975}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "31461327-860d-5375-afd7-a192d9de0764" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B={[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348974} :answer-field/id #uuid "d94578f7-ec3b-515d-b5de-7f5a09965c1f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348970}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d28d774b-78ee-5a83-b15c-27739e6b4b82" :question/math-academy-id "q-74972" :question/problem "Consider the vectors ${a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}],$ and ${a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].$ Find a basis of $S=\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}$  by inspection." :question/worked-solution "Remember that a basis of $S$ is a set of linearly independent vectors that spans $S.$\n\nFrom the given vectors, we can see that ${a}_{2}$ is a linear combination of vectors ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{3}:$\n\n$$\n{a}_{2}=2\\cdot {a}_{1}+0\\cdot {a}_{3}\n$$\n\nConsequently, the vector ${a}_{2}$ can be removed from $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}$ without changing the span. So $S=\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}$ is spanned by just ${{a}_{1},{a}_{3}}.$ \n\nLastly, note that ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{3}$ are linearly independent since they are not parallel. So the set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{3}}$ is a linearly independent set that spans $S.$\n\nTherefore, a basis of $S$ is ${{a}_{1},{a}_{3}},$ that is to say,\n\n$$\nB={{{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{1}},{{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{3}}}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348976 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f892805c-2c2c-5105-91ba-353aefe7b7f2" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Basis of the Space Spanned by a Set of Vectors Using Inspection"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cba7c8b4-30a4-5a94-ad53-f8dc00e88c1a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B={[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348978} {:answer/id #uuid "34a86d49-5574-550b-b0ea-570a5dd92dea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B={[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348979} {:answer/id #uuid "796d28cc-890e-5e92-8a4b-bf71b7be946a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B={[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348980} {:answer/id #uuid "9560bf2d-b1c9-578c-8ab5-b4bd06f31fdc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B={[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348981} {:answer/id #uuid "58cf4930-b47f-5673-a6ff-2c83533f2259" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B={[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348982}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "34a86d49-5574-550b-b0ea-570a5dd92dea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B={[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348979} :answer-field/id #uuid "916fae29-9600-5cb8-a665-4caba0fc753d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348977}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "87a94cdf-c793-5534-931c-84a973feddef" :question/math-academy-id "q-74973" :question/problem "Consider the vectors ${a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],$ and ${a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$ Find a basis of $S=\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}$ by inspection." :question/worked-solution "Remember that a basis of $S$ is a set of linearly independent vectors that spans $S.$\n\nFrom the given vectors, we can see that ${a}_{2}$ is a linear combination of vectors ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{3}:$\n\n$$\n{a}_{2}=2\\cdot {a}_{1}+0\\cdot {a}_{3}\n$$\n\nConsequently, the vector ${a}_{2}$ can be removed from $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}$ without changing the span. So $S=\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}$ is spanned by just ${{a}_{1},{a}_{3}}.$ \n\nLastly, note that ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{3}$ are linearly independent since they are not parallel. So the set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{3}}$ is a linearly independent set that spans $S.$\n\nTherefore, a basis of $S$ is ${{a}_{1},{a}_{3}},$ that is to say,\n\n$$\nB={{{[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{1}},{{[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{3}}}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348983 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6f644bed-7adb-5907-87b4-99b1902e7850" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Basis of the Space Spanned by a Set of Vectors by Identifying Pivot Columns"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ac42e78f-64bb-585c-b7c9-e3c655a04a53" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B={[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348985} {:answer/id #uuid "eca0194e-300f-5258-bf49-19ea7c725c2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B={[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348986} {:answer/id #uuid "28c8de76-f1e1-5814-8845-f5ba1ad4cfac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B={[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348987} {:answer/id #uuid "3fd310b0-2fc2-522b-b3b9-32ac49b4a2a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B={[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348988} {:answer/id #uuid "3595d1da-bc78-5c85-8d01-bae36894af9d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B={[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ 16\\end{aligned}]}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348989}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ac42e78f-64bb-585c-b7c9-e3c655a04a53" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B={[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348985} :answer-field/id #uuid "396363a6-ab56-57a5-b948-c3590c2ac1a3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348984}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9a90968f-6d5f-5ad5-b488-01f80de8a4e6" :question/math-academy-id "q-74979" :question/problem "Consider the vectors ${a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],$ ${a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ 16\\end{aligned}],$ and ${a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].$ Find a basis $B$ of $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}.$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find a subset of linearly independent vectors. So, we start by creating a matrix whose columns are made up of our vectors, and then we reduce the matrix to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}3 & 12 & 6 \\\\ 4 & 16 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 16 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe pivot columns correspond to linearly independent vectors, while the non-pivot columns correspond to linearly dependent vectors that can be removed. Here, the $1$st and $3$rd columns are pivot columns, while the $2$nd column is a non-pivot column.\n\nRemember that we need to pick the pivot columns from the *original matrix*, not from the reduced one.\n\nThe $1$st and $3$rd columns from the original matrix are ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{3}.$ So, a basis of $S$ is ${{a}_{1},{a}_{3}},$ that is to say, \n\n$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348990 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6f644bed-7adb-5907-87b4-99b1902e7850" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Basis of the Space Spanned by a Set of Vectors by Identifying Pivot Columns"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "68623634-3a2f-5cc9-88ff-f5418cd6f11f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B={[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ -9 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348992} {:answer/id #uuid "8282941f-6e9e-5fda-8edd-c3d0e71dbd75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B={[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348993} {:answer/id #uuid "98fad079-d0c6-536f-9d4c-a22d176357ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B={[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ -9 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348994} {:answer/id #uuid "c2c19441-8ec8-5767-a273-759b980b02c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B={[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348995} {:answer/id #uuid "0b66a55d-97fc-56b3-9fe6-cb519b1b4429" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B={[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348996}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c2c19441-8ec8-5767-a273-759b980b02c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B={[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348995} :answer-field/id #uuid "f5411f35-61f7-52af-8acd-57830b7f3cbc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348991}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cc9df4ad-005d-5987-ba45-18fb5548627d" :question/math-academy-id "q-74981" :question/problem "Consider the vectors ${a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],$ ${a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],$ and ${a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ -9 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$ Find a basis $B$ of $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}.$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find a subset of linearly independent vectors. So, we start by creating a matrix whose columns are made up of our vectors, and then we reduce the matrix to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, our matrix is already in a row echelon form.\n\nThe pivot columns correspond to linearly independent vectors, while the non-pivot columns correspond to linearly dependent vectors that can be removed. Here, the $1$st and $2$nd columns are pivot columns, while the $3$rd column is a non-pivot column.\n\nThe $1$st and $2$nd columns from the original matrix are ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}.$ So, a basis of $S$ is ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}},$ that is to say, \n\n$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120451 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b72ed196-a73b-59ab-a7c3-5173249cf7e5" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Given Set Is a Basis of a Span"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "218a1a93-1f3b-52b9-937c-625ff59c376a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348998} {:answer/id #uuid "0dccfdbe-6159-50cc-91ad-cf3d3fc25136" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}$ is not a basis of $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3},{a}_{4}}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348999} {:answer/id #uuid "78473c31-5180-5e5c-925d-466b63fc73e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349000} {:answer/id #uuid "4dbba0a6-46e6-5b55-8970-de419896a86d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349001} {:answer/id #uuid "b34c4c16-5919-5414-8463-159401f05824" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349002}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b34c4c16-5919-5414-8463-159401f05824" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349002} :answer-field/id #uuid "1cb5d2a4-f07b-549c-bd80-bc4c50f63d95" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348997}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "1c72b3a4-9e18-57da-90d5-8d38d6a9dad9" :question/math-academy-id "q-75588" :question/problem "The vectors ${a}_{1},$ ${a}_{2},$ ${a}_{3},$ and ${a}_{4}$ are given below. Determine whether $B={{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3},{a}_{4}}.$ If that is the case, find ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3},$ where ${a}_{4}={x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}.$\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{4}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We want to determine if $B$ is indeed a basis of $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3},{a}_{4}}.$ So, we want to find ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3}\\in R$ such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{1}}+{x}_{2}{{[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{2}}+{x}_{3}{{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{3}}={{[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{4}}.\n$$\n\nThis equation is equivalent to the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=-1 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}=2 \\\\ 5{x}_{1}-5{x}_{2}+6{x}_{3}=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we reduce the augmented matrix of the system to reduced row echelon form (RREF):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 3 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 5 & -5 & 6 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 5 & -5 & 6 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-5){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 7\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-1){R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 7\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the reduced matrix above, we see that the pivot columns are the $1$st, $2$nd, and $3$rd columns. So,  $B$ is indeed a basis of $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3},{a}_{4}}.$\nAlso, the matrix tells us that ${x}_{1}=-8,$ ${x}_{2}=0,$ and ${x}_{3}=7,$ meaning that\n\n$$\n(-8)\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{1}}+0\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{2}}+7\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{3}}={{[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{4}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=-8+0+7=-1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186349003 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b72ed196-a73b-59ab-a7c3-5173249cf7e5" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Given Set Is a Basis of a Span"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9aba64fe-a0af-5801-a808-4da19bd5da59" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349005} {:answer/id #uuid "f579d489-c656-584a-b3c4-7dcd5d4bf8e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349006} {:answer/id #uuid "61632226-f1f4-5a81-9b93-f51b47d619c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349007} {:answer/id #uuid "64aa075a-24a2-5970-9664-1d1befbbbb52" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349008} {:answer/id #uuid "2896cb60-a383-5bb9-93ff-c917bb8e016a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is not a basis of $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349009}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "61632226-f1f4-5a81-9b93-f51b47d619c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349007} :answer-field/id #uuid "fa35db90-0b21-5c1d-a7e7-d80d761721f4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349004}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a474b0ef-b7c4-59e9-85d4-8b00ed5acce4" :question/math-academy-id "q-76322" :question/problem "The vectors ${a}_{1},$ ${a}_{2},$ and ${a}_{3}$ are given below. Determine whether $B={{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}.$ If that is the case, find ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2},$ where ${a}_{3}={x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}.$\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We want to determine if $B$ is indeed a basis of $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}.$ So, we want to find ${x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in R$ such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{1}}+{x}_{2}{{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{2}}={{[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{3}}.\n$$\n\nThis equation is equivalent to the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=8 \\\\ -3{x}_{1}+6{x}_{2}=12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we reduce the augmented matrix of the system to reduced row echelon form (RREF):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 8 \\\\ -3 & 6 & 12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 12 & 36\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{12}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the RREF matrix above, we see that the pivot columns are the $1$st and $2$nd columns. So,  $B$ is indeed a basis of $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}.$\nAlso, the matrix tells us that ${x}_{1}=2$ and ${x}_{2}=3,$ meaning that\n\n$$\n2\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{1}}+3\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{2}}={{[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{3}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=2\\cdot 3=6.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186349010 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b72ed196-a73b-59ab-a7c3-5173249cf7e5" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Given Set Is a Basis of a Span"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "94a6d1f6-41e9-5c64-a297-ba78da7a6452" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349012} {:answer/id #uuid "2a4efa26-98ad-5706-a25d-61600653663a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349013} {:answer/id #uuid "51295dae-777f-55a1-8529-c0bc227cbd80" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is not a basis of $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349014} {:answer/id #uuid "1c27d068-7397-5355-a45a-69157718315d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349015} {:answer/id #uuid "62a5eb31-85f6-5491-bdfb-22164d6d663e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349016}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "94a6d1f6-41e9-5c64-a297-ba78da7a6452" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349012} :answer-field/id #uuid "d8e47fee-aa38-55f7-8077-4f11336ba88b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349011}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "463453a7-4d4a-51d4-b218-335de29d4bcd" :question/math-academy-id "q-76327" :question/problem "The vectors ${a}_{1},$ ${a}_{2},$ and ${a}_{3}$ are given below. Determine whether $B={{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}.$ If that is the case, find ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2},$ where ${a}_{3}={x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}.$\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ -10\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We want to determine if $B$ is indeed a basis of $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}.$ So, we want to find ${x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in R$ such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{1}}+{x}_{2}{{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{2}}={{[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ -10\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{3}}.\n$$\n\nThis equation is equivalent to the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-6 \\\\ {x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=-10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we reduce the augmented matrix of the system to reduced row echelon form (RREF):\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -6 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the RREF matrix above, we see that the pivot columns are the $1$st and $2$nd columns. So,  $B$ is indeed a basis of $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}.$\nAlso, the matrix tells us that ${x}_{1}=-2$ and ${x}_{2}=-4,$ meaning that\n\n$$\n(-2)\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{1}}+(-4)\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{2}}={{[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ -10\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{3}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=(-2)\\cdot (-4)=8.$"}]}
